  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Peroxodisulphate, obtained by electrolytic oxidation of acidified sulphate solutions at high current density, on hydrolysis yields hydrogen peroxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi>HSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mtext>Electrolysis</mtext></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>HO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>SOOSO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mtext>Electrolysis</mtext></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><msub><mi>HSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>This method is now used for the laboratory preparation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>KDSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></math> &nbsp;</p>"
